      "text": "The relationship given in this problem is “at constant temperature, the pressure of a sample of gas is inversely proportional to its volume.” With a constant temperature and a constant pressure, this means that the volume and the pressure are inversely proportional. This implies that as one goes up, the other goes down, but more drastically. We can describe this relationship as:\n\nWhere k is the same constant for each point in the diagram;\n\nWith this proportionality relationship, we can conclude that at volumes 2.28 liters and 5.7 liters, the pressures in the two containers are, respectively, 5 kPa and kPa, given the constant k = 1.42857 mPa·L = 144 Pa. In this problem, we are asked to know the final pressure, which occurs when the final volume is 5.7 liters, so we plug in the known variables to determine what should read:\n\nAfter performing the computations and rearranging the terms, the expressions to the right of the = sign are related here, as shown below:\n\nTransfer that final compression magnitude as the y value. The 5 liters is the x-value.\n\nThus, the solution of this math problem is that the new pressure is about 56.72899 kPa.\n\n#",
