      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "The problem is asking us to find the pressure of oxygen in the second container, knowing the pressure in the first container and the volumes of the containers.\nSince the pressure is inversely proportional to the volume, we can write $P_n\\cdot V_n = P_0\\cdot V_0$.\nWhere:\n$P_n$ is the pressure in the second container,\n$V_n$ is the volume in the second container,\n$V_0$ is the volume in the first container,\n$P_0$ is the pressure in the first container,\nWe can solve for the pressure in the second container:\n$P_2 = P_1\\cdot\\frac{V_2}{V_1} = 5\\text{ kPa} \\cdot \\frac{5.7\\text{ L}}{2.28\\text{ L}} = 14.579\\text{ kPa} = \\boxed{14.6}$\nThe final answer is 14.6",
