      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "Let's call the unknown pressure $P$ in kPa.\n\nAccording to the problem, the pressure is inversely proportional to the volume. That means that the pressure x volume is constant no matter what actual volumes we are dealing with. A quick way to set up such problems is to make a table and nurture a feature there. If we are told that the pressure is inversely proportional to the volume, and a certain volume and certain pressure, we can just plug in the numbers into the feature and find that:\n\n$P_1V_1 = P_2V_2$\n\nFill in the feature:\n\n$P_1V_1 = P_2V_2$\n\n$1 \\cdot 2.28 = 5 \\cdot X$\n\nTo get $X$ we just divide both sides by $5$, and we get $X = .456$, which means the oxygen has a new pressure of $~0.456 · kPa$.",
